We have a fundamental UX issue. We have the concept of keyframes and anchor points, but the user doesn't understand what they are or how to use them. 

They are essentially the same thing. We need to simplify the UI/UX and remove the concept of keyframes. We should just have anchor points, and the user should be able to set an anchor point at any point in time. The anchor points will then be used as a reference point for tracking, and the user can track forwards or backwards from that anchor point.

We might rename these to anything in the future "tracking reference points" or "tracking anchors" etc. but for now we should just remove the concept of keyframes and just have anchor points.

The core concept of the UX is the user should be able to set an anchor point at any point in time, and then track forwards or backwards from that anchor point. The user should also be able to delete anchor points, and the tracking should update accordingly.